---
/**
 * Percent calculator — 캐나다판 첫 도구. 한국어판 /tools/percent/ 와 계산(lib/percent.ts)·스크립트(EN 사전)를 같이 쓰고,
 * 문장은 캐나다 영어로 새로 썼다(번역 아님). 산술이라 나라 제도·rates 와 상관없다(조사표 캐나다 칸 '같음').
 *
 * 소제목은 캐나다 구글 자동완성에서 왔다(keywords/ca-percent-2026-10-20.csv):
 *   percent off calculator (canada · with tax · of $50) / percent increase or decrease formula · between two numbers /
 *   percentage of a number formula / percentage calculator grade · of marks
 * title·description 은 같은 영어 판(en-us·en-gb·en-au·en-sg)과 갈리게 Canada 를 넣었다.
 * 판매세(GST·HST·PST) 세율은 쓰지 않는다 — 주마다 다르고 캐나다 rates 로 검증하지 않았다. 계산 순서만 설명한다.
 */
import BaseHead from "../../../../components/BaseHead.astro";
import AdSlot from "../../../../components/AdSlot.astro";
import ClarityHead from "../../../../components/ClarityHead.astro";
import GtagHead from "../../../../components/GtagHead.astro";
import TrackLinks from "../../../../components/TrackLinks.astro";
import AdSenseHead from "../../../../components/AdSenseHead.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../../../../styles/global.css";

const title = "Percent Calculator Canada — Percent Off, Increase & Decrease, Percentage of a Number";
const description =
  "Percent calculator for Canada: price after a percent off, percent increase or decrease between two numbers, a percentage of a number and test marks.";
---

<html lang="en-CA">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={title} description={description} />
    <ClarityHead />
    <GtagHead />
    <AdSenseHead />
  </head>
  <body class="bg-texture">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main>
      <h1>Percent calculator</h1>
      <p>
        Pick what you are working out and type in two numbers. Answers are rounded to two decimal places.
      </p>

      <div class="calc-card" data-two>
        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label for="mode">What do you want to find?</label>
          <select id="mode" data-seg>
            <option value="ratio" selected>What % of A is B?</option>
            <option value="of">What is B% of A?</option>
            <option value="change">% change from A to B</option>
            <option value="adjust">Add or take B% off A</option>
            <option value="original">Original value before a B% change</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="field" id="dir-row" hidden>
          <label for="dir">Increase or decrease</label>
          <select id="dir" data-seg>
            <option value="down" selected>Decrease (% off)</option>
            <option value="up">Increase</option>
          </select>
        </div>

        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label id="a-label" for="a">Whole value A</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="decimal" id="a" value="200" autocomplete="off" />
        </div>

        <div class="calc-input-wrap">
          <label id="b-label" for="b">Part value B</label>
          <input type="text" inputmode="decimal" id="b" value="50" autocomplete="off" />
          <span class="unit" id="b-unit" hidden>%</span>
        </div>

        <div class="result-hero" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-dock="hero-value">
          <p class="label" id="hero-label">B as a percentage of A</p>
          <p class="big" id="hero-value">25%</p>
          <p class="hint" id="formula">50 ÷ 200 × 100</p>
        </div>

        <div class="stat-row" data-receipt id="receipt">
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label" id="l1">Whole value A</span>
            <span class="value" id="v1">200</span>
          </div>
          <div class="stat-chip">
            <span class="label" id="l2">Part value B</span>
            <span class="value" id="v2">50</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="actions">
          <button id="btn-download" type="button">Save as image</button>
          <button id="btn-share" type="button" class="secondary">Share</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Percent off calculator: price after a discount</h2>
      <p>
        Multiply the price by what is left after the discount. 25% off $80.00 leaves 75%, so the sale price is
        $80.00 × 0.75 = $60.00 and you save $20.00. For 30% off $50.00 it is $50.00 × 0.70 = $35.00. Pick
        "Add or take B% off A", set it to decrease and enter the price and the percent.
      </p>
      <p>
        Going backwards needs a division, not a multiplication. If a jacket is $68.00 after 15% off, the tag price
        was $68.00 ÷ 0.85 = $80.00. The "Original value before a B% change" option does this.
      </p>

      <h2>Percent off with tax</h2>
      <p>
        Sales tax in Canada depends on the province or territory, so this calculator does not add any tax by itself.
        Work it out in two steps: take the discount off first, then use "Add or take B% off A" set to increase with
        the combined tax rate for where you are shopping. Each step multiplies the price, so doing them in the other
        order gives the same total.
      </p>

      <h2>Percent increase or decrease formula</h2>
      <p>
        Subtract the starting value from the new value, divide by the starting value, then multiply by 100.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Increase</strong> — rent going from $1,600 to $1,720 is (1,720 − 1,600) ÷ 1,600 × 100 = +7.5%.</li>
        <li><strong>Decrease</strong> — a bill dropping from $120 to $90 is (90 − 120) ÷ 120 × 100 = −25%.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The starting value is always the one you divide by. That is why going from $90 back up to $120 is a 33.33%
        increase, not 25%.
      </p>

      <h2>Percentage of a number formula</h2>
      <p>
        Turn the percent into a decimal and multiply: 12% of 450 is 450 × 0.12 = 54. To find what percent one number
        is of another, divide the part by the whole and multiply by 100 — 18 out of 24 is 18 ÷ 24 × 100 = 75%.
      </p>

      <h2>Percentage calculator for grades and marks</h2>
      <p>
        A test mark works the same way: marks earned ÷ marks possible × 100. 42 out of 56 is 75%. Enter the total
        as A and your mark as B with "What % of A is B?". Adding up percentages from separate tests does not give
        your overall grade unless every test is worth the same number of marks — add the marks first, then divide.
      </p>

      <details>
        <summary>Why doesn't a 20% increase followed by a 20% decrease get back to the start?</summary>
        <p>
          The second 20% is taken from a bigger number. 100 plus 20% is 120, and 20% off 120 is 120 × 0.8 = 96. To
          return to 100 from 120 you only need to take off 16.67%, which the "Original value" option shows.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Is percent change the same as percent difference?</summary>
        <p>
          No. Percent change has a before and an after and divides by the before value. Percent difference treats
          the two numbers equally and divides the gap by their average. This calculator gives percent change: from
          40 to 60 is +50%, and from 60 to 40 is −33.33%.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What if the starting value is negative or zero?</summary>
        <p>
          The calculator divides by the size of the starting value without its minus sign, so moving up always reads
          as an increase: a loss going from −200 to −150 is +25%. With a starting value of 0 there is nothing to
          divide by, so only the difference is shown.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>What is the difference between a percent and a percentage point?</summary>
        <p>
          When a rate moves from 4% to 5%, it went up by <strong>1 percentage point</strong>. Compared with where it
          started, that is a (5 − 4) ÷ 4 × 100 = <strong>25%</strong> increase. Points measure the gap between two
          percentages; percent change measures how big that gap is relative to the first one.
        </p>
      </details>

      <AdSlot label="percent-result-en-ca" />
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
    <script src="../../../../scripts/percent.ts"></script>
    <TrackLinks />
    <script src="../../../../scripts/calc-ui.ts"></script>
  </body>
</html>
